              "A design class studied the {{life cycle}} of a shoe, from its manufacture to the day someone no longer wanted it. Passing a usable pair to another wearer was reuse. Damaged pairs might need {{reprocessing}}, in which the material was changed before being made into something else.",
              "That was difficult with a {{composite}} sole whose different materials were stuck together. The students designed a version with {{detachable}} parts that could be separated more easily. They also proposed a {{collection point}} at the sports centre so that people would know where to leave unwanted pairs."
