            "paragraphs": [
              "A reading group explored a {{microbiome}} rather than imagine every microbe living alone. Microbes were described as {{ubiquitous}}. The idea of a {{holobiont}} treated an organism and its microbes as a combined unit, but did not make every interaction identical.",
              "A microbe in the gut could have a different effect if it entered the bloodstream. Calling it good or bad {{out of context}} could therefore be misleading. A {{symbiotic}} relationship might be {{mutually beneficial}} in one situation or {{mutually destructive}} in another.",
              "Research tried to {{unravel}} roles in {{digestion}} and interactions with the {{immune system}}. A test of one toxin addressed a narrower question than the health of the whole community. The group welcomed the detail while keeping the setting visible: a useful result about one relationship did not establish the same effect for every organism, body part or possible intervention."
            ]
