            "paragraphs": [
              "Wisdom was a revered quality in the reading group’s discussion. The group wanted {{empirical}} evidence rather than assume one person was always wise in every setting. An {{experiential}} influence came from past events, while a {{situational}} one belonged to the circumstances at hand.",
              "A {{contextual factor}} could change a response to an unresolved issue. Someone with a {{personal stake}} might focus on one immediate concern. Another perspective could help identify a possible {{compromise}} or {{integration}} of views that had seemed incompatible.",
              "The group valued {{intellectual humility}}: a careful person could recognise a limit without abandoning every judgement. A trait described as {{agreeableness}} might relate to how people interacted, but a friendly manner was not identical to reasoning wisely. The same person could show more or less careful judgement as the problem, relationships and way of looking at the situation changed."
            ]
