            "paragraphs": [
              "A guide discussed an imaginary {{amphitheatre}} as part of {{urban architecture}}. It had hosted a public spectacle, then taken on other uses. Becoming a fortress was one possible stage in the fictional history, not proof that every such building followed the same sequence.",
              "A {{versatile}} building could change its role without disappearing. Older parts might remain {{embedded}} in later work and become {{absorbed into}} the {{fabric}} of a neighbourhood. The guide asked visitors to distinguish retaining a structure from retaining its first use.",
              "The building did not necessarily {{revert to}} its original function. Its {{acoustics}} could make it useful for a new kind of performance. Falling into disuse was also different from falling into {{disrepair}}: a closed place might still be cared for, while an open one might need repairs. The group recorded uses and physical condition separately rather than assume one word explained both."
            ]
