            "paragraphs": [
              "A class visited a display about an {{ancient settlement}}. A {{manuscript}} could survive as one fragment rather than an entire work. A {{scroll}} was stored in a roll, while other texts had different forms. The guide asked students to record the object before guessing what all its writing meant.",
              "One label identified {{parchment}} and another {{papyrus}}. A worker might {{chisel}} marks into a harder surface so they could better {{withstand}} handling. A different material did not by itself reveal a different author, language or purpose.",
              "The archive worked to preserve what remained and {{reassemble}} separate pieces. Scholars still needed to {{decipher}} the writing. Recognising an {{alphabet}} was not the same as translating every word, and putting the pieces together did not automatically solve the message. The class kept physical repair and interpretation as related but distinct kinds of work."
            ]
