            "paragraphs": [
              "A class read an account of a fictional {{marsupial}}. A {{superficial resemblance}} to another animal did not establish close ancestry. The guide used a {{distinguishing feature}} for identification and kept temperament separate from appearance. Similar-looking animals could behave differently.",
              "The account compared different terrain and identified a {{prime habitat}}. It described a {{carnivorous}} diet and an organ able to {{distend}} after feeding. This might {{compensate for}} long gaps without food, but the class noted that the explanation was a possibility rather than an observed purpose.",
              "The animal may have depended on {{pursuit}} rather than a brief burst of speed. It could retreat to shelter by day and was mainly {{nocturnal}}. One daytime observation did not erase the usual pattern. The students separated general tendencies, unusual sightings and suggested explanations so that a small exception would not be mistaken for a complete contradiction."
            ]
