            "paragraphs": [
              "A historical database brought together an {{inventory}}, a tax entry and a family record. The inventory listed {{worldly goods}}. An asset did not provide a full measure of wealth if debt was ignored, so the team compared several documents instead of count possessions alone.",
              "A mark on a page could offer an {{indicator}} of literacy, while another task gave clues about {{numeracy}}. Neither one item nor one signature necessarily measured the whole of education. The group also considered {{industriousness}} and the activities connected with the objects listed.",
              "Through {{demographic reconstruction}}, researchers linked records about one person and a descendant over time. A court entry might {{chastise}} someone for an action and reveal a restriction affecting their life. This did not tell the whole story by itself. The strength of the collection came from putting several kinds of evidence about the same people into a shared account."
            ]
