            "paragraphs": [
              "A player wore a blindfold while opponents could see their own boards. Managing several games simultaneously was a {{mental feat}}. To an {{uninitiated}} visitor, it seemed impossible, but an {{accomplished}} player could {{run through}} meaningful patterns using experience with the game.",
              "The challenge involved more than the first act of memorising. The player had to {{retrieve}} an earlier position, recall it {{faithfully}}, update it after a move and keep it ready while turning to another board. A mistake at one stage could affect later decisions.",
              "The task became {{taxing}} as the session continued. Recall could turn {{patchy}} rather than disappear completely. The club admired the player’s {{prowess}} while recognising the effort and the limits. A striking skill in this setting did not automatically establish equally strong performance on every other memory task or explain precisely how the ability had developed."
            ]
