            "paragraphs": [
              "A class compared a concrete sample with a wood-based panel. The teacher explained that cement was one ingredient, not a second name for the entire material. Availability mattered too: a useful recipe could be hard to adopt if its ingredients were not present in {{abundance}}.",
              "One mix was {{pourable}} and {{mouldable}} before being left to set. The class then compared {{thermal expansion}} and considered how to reinforce it. Another sample was made from {{cross-laminated timber}}, using an {{adhesive}} to join pieces in different directions.",
              "The class tested more than initial strength. A sample might be {{susceptible}} to one kind of damage even if it performed well in another test. Good {{durability}} meant remaining useful over time. No single result supplied a complete answer, so the students recorded the conditions of each test rather than call one material best for every possible building."
            ]
