            "paragraphs": [
              "A school discussed {{streaming}} after a set of assessments. Current {{attainment}} showed what learners had done, but it was not a complete measure of {{aptitude}}. A {{selective}} approach used entry criteria, while a {{comprehensive}} school taught pupils across a wider range.",
              "Each stakeholder had concerns. One critic used an analogy and predicted {{mediocrity}} if everyone stayed together. The argument was {{intuitively}} attractive to some listeners, but the committee asked for {{empirical}} evidence rather than decide from the comparison alone.",
              "The review considered {{socioeconomic}} differences as well as scores. It also asked whether a label could {{entrench}} a teacher’s expectation. This did not mean an assessment was useless. It meant the school needed to distinguish a record of present performance from a claim about what a learner could achieve with a different task, more time or better support."
            ]
