            "paragraphs": [
              "A reading group examined a claim that people always act from self-interest. The claim was {{prevalent}}, but that did not settle whether it was true. A helpful action might have an {{ulterior motive}}, yet the group could not assume one without evidence. It also discussed {{altruism}} and cases in which people gave up something to help others.",
              "The article asked whether a {{ruthless}} tendency was {{innate}} or shaped by conditions. A prehistoric community in a {{sparsely populated}} area might face different pressures from a crowded settlement. Assuming {{scarcity}} everywhere would make an argument seem stronger than its evidence allowed.",
              "The {{advent}} of a new way of living could change relationships. However, a contemporary example could not automatically reveal every detail of the distant past. The group wanted a {{feasible}} explanation supported by evidence. It also asked whether people could {{transcend}} a habit, even if that habit was common in their own setting."
            ]
