            "paragraphs": [
              "Our town once had several small cloth workshops. Sewing provided a livelihood for many families. Later, a large {{corporation}} opened a {{dedicated}} factory outside town. It had more {{capital}} to spend on equipment, but some finishing work remained {{labour-intensive}}. A change in ownership did not automatically change every task.",
              "The council proposed to {{subsidise}} training at the factory. Some shop owners worried that public money would keep its costs {{artificially}} low. They asked who might {{come off worse}} if small workshops lost their orders. Others wanted a {{trade barrier}} against cheaper imports, but that could also raise prices for local buyers.",
              "A historian reminded the meeting that one business {{dynasty}} had controlled much of the trade in the past. She compared the old {{labour regime}} with current working conditions. The {{abolition}} of an unfair hiring rule had helped some workers, while other practices showed surprising {{continuity}}. Indeed, {{contrary to}} the idea that every change was entirely new, firms still chose to {{retain}} several old methods."
            ]
