              "A {{conservation}} group examined a plan for {{logging}} near the reserve. They worried that new roads would {{fragment}} the woodland and remove quiet places used for {{hibernation}}. Protecting trees only in small separate patches might not be enough.",
              "The group also asked for limits on fishing, rather than {{unrestricted}} catches. A decline in food could make successful {{reproduction}} harder. Their final proposal was to expand the protected area while keeping a connected route between feeding places."
